  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prevention Information Lutte contre le Sida (PILS) - Mauritius (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritius, HIV, Pr&#xe9;vention Information Lutte contre le Sida (PILS)This program has the following goals: Reduction in AIDS-related mortality.  Stabilisation of HIV prevalence among Key Population (people who inject drugs (PWID), Men having Sex with Men (MSM), Transgender people (TG), and Sex Workers (SW)). The objectives of this program are: Provide ART to 70% of PLHIV eligible to ART and ensure 90% of PLHIV on ART adherent after 12 months.  Provide voluntary HIV testing to 60% of combined mapped key populations.  Reach 30% of mapped transgendered people with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reach 45% of mapped MSM with HIV prevention education and material.  Reach 50% of mapped sex workers with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reach 80% of mapped PWID with HIV prevention education and materials.  Reduction in AIDS-related mortality.  Stabilisation of HIV prevalence among people who inject drugs</narrative>
  </description>
